# BetterWorld Trivy Ignore List
# These CVEs are acknowledged false positives or non-exploitable in our context.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# esbuild Go binary CVEs (dev tool binaries compiled with old Go stdlib)
# esbuild is a JavaScript bundler — these Go stdlib network/crypto/archive
# vulnerabilities are not reachable through esbuild's usage pattern.
# Affected: @esbuild/linux-x64@0.18.20, 0.19.12, 0.21.5
# Source: drizzle-kit, vitest (dev dependencies)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CVE-2023-39325
CVE-2023-44487
CVE-2023-45283
CVE-2023-45288
CVE-2024-24790
CVE-2024-34156
CVE-2025-47907
CVE-2025-58183
CVE-2025-61726
CVE-2025-61728
CVE-2025-61729
CVE-2025-61730
CVE-2025-68121

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# System npm tar CVEs (from node:22-slim base image /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/)
# tar is only used during `pnpm install` (build time), not at application runtime.
# Our app's lockfile already overrides tar to >=7.5.8 for our own dependencies.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# System glob CVE (from node:22-slim base image npm)
# glob is used by npm internals, not by our application at runtime.
# Our lockfile already resolves glob to 10.5.0+ for our own dependencies.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CVE-2025-64756

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pnpm CLI CVEs (installed via corepack in Docker image)
# These affect pnpm's lockfile integrity and tokenHelper features.
# Only relevant during `pnpm install` (build time), not at runtime.
# Cannot upgrade to pnpm v10 without major migration.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CVE-2025-69262
CVE-2025-69263
